## Goal
Stop the `portero serve` API from hanging when the rules file is offloaded by iCloud (present in iCloud Drive but not downloaded on this Mac), and trigger the download instead. This came out of a cross-review.

## Problems
None.

## Decision
Added two optional hooks to `serve.Options` in `internal/serve/serve.go`: `Offloaded(path) bool` and `Download(path) error`. `cmd/portero/serve.go` wires them to `sync.Offloaded` and `startDownload`.

In `internal/serve/api.go`, `readRules` and `handleApply` first call `offloadedErr`. If the file is offloaded, it requests the download and returns `errOffloaded`. A new `readFail` helper maps that error to 503 (retry later) and any other read error to 500. `handleState`, `handleValidate`, `handleMatch` and `handleApply` use it.

The check runs before any read, so no handler blocks on a dataless file. Nil hooks disable the behaviour, so tests and non-iCloud setups are unaffected.

`handleMatch` returns 503 for an offloaded file. Other read failures there keep the existing 422 "no rules file" answer.

`TestOffloadedRulesAnswer503WithoutReading` checks that all four endpoints return 503 and that the download is requested once per call.

## Rejected
None.

## Touched
iCloud Drive (offloaded rules file download), `sync.Offloaded`, `startDownload`, `serve.Options`, the `internal/serve` HTTP API.
